Not sure why you are using the weird, unnecessary piping operator from the Hadley-Wickham-verse, but it seems you are using it incorrectly.  The call is passing your model to the data= argument.  I assume jes3A_D is your data.frame?  Try following the format shown by the developer in the lavaan tutorial:

crossA_D <- sem(model_jes3, data = jes3A_D, ordered = c("PARTY1","ELECTION1", "CONGRESS1", "INFLU1", "COMPLEX1", "NOCARE1", "PARTY2","ELECTION2", "CONGRESS2", "INFLU2", "COMPLEX2", "NOCARE2"))

