1. Confidence intervals for the intercepts of N_TOL of the Female group did not include positive values.
2. Estimates for the intercepts of the subscales of the Males group were not calculated.

After reading a couple of threads, I have come up with 2 solutions (other than increasing the sample size for males):
1. Because the eigenvalue is close to zero, we may move on.
2. Report the model fit and the confidence intervals.

Which solution is more ideal?

Thank you.

