Further, there's excellent reason for that to be the default in lavaan (as Terrence said, "makes sense to free"), as it is in most software I have used. Leaving that covariance fixed to zero is an explicit hypothesis that the observed covariance between DV1 and DV2 is entirely accounted for by their antecedents in the model, in this case Med2. In most practical situations, that would be quite a strong declaration.

